        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(imessage): remove split-send coalescing config",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes #91243. Replaces #107182 with a clean branch based on current `main` after the old PR became noisy/conflicted.\n\nThe iMessage plugin still exposed OpenClaw-side split-send coalescing config even though current `imsg` owns Apple URL-preview coalescing before OpenClaw receives messages. That left stale config/default surface area and confused upgrade proof.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n- Removes the retired `channels.imessage.coalesceSameSenderDms` config/default/schema surface and the iMessage-specific URL-preview bucket policy.\n- Keeps the generic inbound debounce merge helper for configured `messages.inbound` batching, with narrow caps and tests.\n- Adds iMessage doctor legacy rules so `openclaw doctor --fix` removes retired root/account keys.\n- Lets doctor repair plugin-owned legacy config before strict runtime reads, without masking unrelated malformed plugin config.\n- Refreshes generated config, bundled channel metadata, and Plugin SDK API baselines.\n- Splits existing daemon restart health diagnostics/listener tests so the whole-core lint shard passes max-lines without adding forbidden suppressions or import cycles.\n\n## User Impact\n\nExisting users no longer need or see the retired iMessage coalescing knob. Users upgrading with stale `coalesceSameSenderDms` config get a doctor repair path instead of runtime fallback behavior. Malformed non-legacy plugin config still fails closed and can recover from last-known-good during doctor repair.\n\n## Evidence\n\nExact head: `a5aaf05cd93b422094be4d22ffab4dbafb9150c7`.\n\n- `git diff --check` passed.\n- `node --import tsx scripts/generate-config-doc-baseline.ts --check` passed: `OK docs/.generated/config-baseline.sha256`.\n- `node --import tsx scripts/generate-bundled-channel-config-metadata.ts --check` passed.\n- `node --import tsx scripts/generate-base-config-schema.ts --check` passed: `[base-config-schema] ok`.\n- `node --max-old-space-size=8192 --import tsx scripts/generate-plugin-sdk-api-baseline.ts --check` passed: `OK docs/.generated/plugin-sdk-api-baseline.sha256`.\n- `./node_modules/.bin/oxlint src/cli/daemon-cli/restart-health.ts src/cli/daemon-cli/restart-health-diagnostics.ts src/cli/daemon-cli/restart-health-types.ts src/cli/daemon-cli/restart-health.test.ts src/cli/daemon-cli/restart-health-listener.test.ts` passed.\n- `node scripts/check-madge-import-cycles.ts` passed: `Madge import cycle check: 0 cycle(s).`\n- `node scripts/check-max-lines-ratchet.mjs --base origin/main` passed: `max-lines ratchet OK: 1187 grandfathered suppressions.`\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/cli/daemon-cli/restart-health.test.ts src/cli/daemon-cli/restart-health-listener.test.ts src/config/config.legacy-config-detection.accepts-imessage-dmpolicy.test.ts src/commands/doctor-config-preflight.test.ts extensions/imessage/src/doctor-contract-api.test.ts extensions/imessage/src/status.test.ts` passed 4 Vitest shards, 6 files, 119 tests.\n- Local macOS `imsg --version` is `0.12.3`; `imsg status --json` reports 28 RPC methods and `watch.subscribe` support.\n- Exact-head isolated upgrade proof: with `OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR` and `OPENCLAW_CONFIG_PATH` pointed at a temp config containing both `channels.imessage.coalesceSameSenderDms` and `channels.imessage.accounts.work.coalesceSameSenderDms`, `pnpm openclaw doctor --fix --non-interactive --yes` exited `0`. Before: `{root:true, account:true}`. After: `{root:false, account:false}`. Doctor output included `Removed retired channels.imessage.coalesceSameSenderDms.` and `Removed retired channels.imessage.accounts.work.coalesceSameSenderDms.`\n- Blacksmith Testbox dependency lane before the final rebase stayed green: `tbx_01kxp3eqw0967s3vcmdjfq2vpe`, run https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29524645499.\n- GitHub CI is rerunning on `a5aaf05cd93b422094be4d22ffab4dbafb9150c7` after the final rebase and CI-lint/import-cycle fixes.\n- Autoreview before the branch rebuild: `.agents/skills/autoreview/scripts/autoreview --mode branch --base origin/main` clean; no accepted/actionable findings.\n\nKnown remaining live-proof limit: this local macOS host has `imsg` available, but the active OpenClaw iMessage config is allowlist-only with no configured iMessage DMs, so I did not collect a new exact-head live inbound command-plus-URL send into OpenClaw. This PR removes OpenClaw-side split-send policy/config and relies on focused unit/doctor/config proof plus the `imsg >= 0.11.1` ownership boundary documented here for the split-send behavior.\n",
        "branch": "agent/imessage-coalescing-clean-91243",
